Higgsfield Genjutsu lets you replace characters in any video using reference images — and in this tutorial, I walk you through the full workflow. I pulled a clip from the 1997 Odyssey miniseries, generated two new character sheets in ChatGPT, built a detailed Genjutsu prompt using a Claude skill I created, and let Higgsfield swap the cast entirely. I also cover the exact upload order that makes the auto-tagging work, credit cost at 720p, and how to grab the Claude skill I built so you don't have to write the prompt yourself.
 
📌 CHAPTERS
00:46 — Generating replacement characters in ChatGPT
01:27 — Designing the second character (Viking with red hair)
01:47 — Use case: restoring old footage with a new cast
02:41 — Setting up Genjutsu: video + reference images
04:04 — Why a prompt gets better results
04:16 — The Claude skill: how it builds your Genjutsu prompt
05:14 — What to give Claude and how to phrase it
05:59 — Upload order: assets first, then paste the prompt

